{
  "kind": "not-adopted-native-load-boundary-experiment",
  "recordedAt": "2026-10-29T04:37:05.278741+08:00",
  "decision": "do-not-adopt; root requested exact rollback",
  "experimentalCatalogVersion": "41614f5714fb815496ca5eb22dc5b8dc6f7c95b7fa92ad4a21cd955356962455",
  "baselineCatalogVersion": "9ba070328a0cce53691378e6a631c0239b5a7f9f926ad61504e8c1da4e4f0405",
  "build": "passed; 58 prerendered routes",
  "scope": "Static build / manifest / byte inspection only; no new browser, simulator, startup timing, room, account or production verification",
  "findings": [
    "Lazy Header client loader boundary does not prevent static prerender HTML modulepreloading its Header/Reka code; modulepreload count increases 23 to 25.",
    "SSO exchange implementation moves out of the eager entry chunk, reducing entry bytes, but that is not proof of startup latency improvement.",
    "The conservative exporter traverses non-entry dynamic imports; the separated identity module now adds CloudBase SDK to every game preparation manifest, plus 3 resources / 741590 bytes each.",
    "No new timing or real authentication proof was attempted; 30 percent engineering target is not met by this experiment.",
    "Keep existing shared route and resource policy; do not expand routes or weaken integrity checks for a passing number."
  ],
